From: Vyron Code D-11 local hardening (VYRON_CODE_D11_PATCH_0005 - ephemeral success-path usage/session writes)
Applies to: NousResearch/hermes-agent, installed local copy, version 0.21.0, ON TOP OF patches
0001, 0002 and 0004 (all three must already be applied; verified present 2026-09-24).

NOT APPLIED BY THIS TOOLING. Generated from `diff -u` of the real installed source against a patched
copy; every edited file parses as valid Python; four of the seven guards were exercised in isolation
(ephemeral agent writes nothing, normal agent behaves exactly as before); `git apply --check` was run
against the real installed Hermes root. Nothing was written to the installed source.

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS (live-proven 2026-09-24 10:52, first successful completion on this machine):
a successful API Server task through OmniRoute wrote one row into `sessions` (api session id,
api_call_count, input/output tokens, model, billing provider and base URL) and one row into
`session_model_usage`, plus WAL bytes. `_ensure_db_session()` was already suppressed by patch 0001, but
`agent/turn_usage.py` calls `queue_token_counts()`, which upserts BOTH rows by itself, and it never
consulted `_persist_disabled`. The error path never reaches this code (a failed call has no usage), so
only a real success could expose it.

WHAT THIS PATCH CHANGES (7 hunks, 7 files; each carries the marker VYRON_LOCAL_PATCH_0005):
  agent/turn_usage.py              the write that created the rows (queue_token_counts + ensure)
  agent/codex_runtime.py           same accounting write for the codex_responses api mode
  agent/session_persistence.py     flush_token_counts() drain at every persist point
  agent/turn_facade.py             ambient accounting context; a None handle clears it, so auxiliary-call
                                   usage (title/vision/compression/...) is never recorded to the session
  agent/conversation_loop.py       update_system_prompt(): writes system_prompts BEFORE its UPDATE, even
                                   when no sessions row exists
  agent/agent_runtime_helpers.py   update_session_billing_route() (provider / base_url after a model switch)
  agent/background_review.py       review-fork usage recorded against the parent session

  Scope: every guard is conditional on `getattr(agent, "_persist_disabled", False)`, which only patch 0001
  sets (API Server agents). Normal Hermes Desktop / TUI / gateway-platform agents have the flag False, so
  their session, usage, billing and debug behaviour is unchanged.

FOUND BUT DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED (unreachable for the D-11 request contract, documented for honesty):
  - Context-compression writes (archive_and_compact, publish_compression_child, ...): triggered only by
    context size; D-11 tasks are capped at 4,000 characters.
  - gateway/platforms/api_server.py `record_gateway_session_peer` / `update_session_runtime_lock`: run only
    when a client sends X-Hermes-Session-Key or requests a model lock; the D-11 request sends neither, and
    both are UPDATE statements (no-op without a row).
  - Auto-title generation: api_server.py never calls it.
  - gateway_heartbeats and similar process-level tables: no task data.
  The stray `api-...` rows written by the 2026-09-24 test are NOT deleted by this patch (kept as
  pre-patch evidence).

HOW TO APPLY (PowerShell, as the user who owns the Hermes installation; nothing below prints credentials).
Stop the running gateway first.

  # 1) Backup: one timestamped .bak next to each of the seven files
  $root  = "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent"
  $files = "agent\turn_usage.py","agent\codex_runtime.py","agent\session_persistence.py","agent\turn_facade.py","agent\conversation_loop.py","agent\agent_runtime_helpers.py","agent\background_review.py"
  $ts = Get-Date -Format "yyyyMMdd_HHmmss"
  foreach ($f in $files) { Copy-Item "$root\$f" "$root\$f.vyron-pre-0005-$ts.bak" }

  # 2) Dry run, then apply. Run from INSIDE the Hermes root (it is itself a git repository);
  #    do not use --directory, it fails on Windows paths.
  Set-Location $root
  git apply --check "D:\Vyron Code\hermes-patches\0005-api-server-ephemeral-success-usage.patch"
  if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { git apply "D:\Vyron Code\hermes-patches\0005-api-server-ephemeral-success-usage.patch" } else { Write-Warning "dry run failed - nothing applied" }

HOW TO VERIFY IT ACTUALLY APPLIED (run BEFORE restarting Hermes):

  $root = "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent"
  $py   = "$root\venv\Scripts\python.exe"
  $ok   = $true
  # patch 0005: one marker + one distinctive code fragment per file
  $p5 = @(
    @("agent\turn_usage.py",              'and not getattr(agent, "_persist_disabled", False):'),
    @("agent\codex_runtime.py",           'getattr(agent, "_persist_disabled", False) or not (agent._session_db'),
    @("agent\session_persistence.py",     'not getattr(self, "_persist_disabled", False):'),
    @("agent\turn_facade.py",             'None if getattr(self, "_persist_disabled", False) else getattr(self, "_session_db", None)'),
    @("agent\conversation_loop.py",       'if not agent._session_db or getattr(agent, "_persist_disabled", False):'),
    @("agent\agent_runtime_helpers.py",   'session_id or getattr(agent, "_persist_disabled", False):'),
    @("agent\background_review.py",       'getattr(parent_agent, "_persist_disabled", False)')
  )
  foreach ($c in $p5) {
    $m = @(Select-String -Path "$root\$($c[0])" -Pattern "VYRON_LOCAL_PATCH_0005" -SimpleMatch).Count
    $h = Select-String -Path "$root\$($c[0])" -Pattern $c[1] -SimpleMatch -Quiet
    if ($m -ne 1 -or -not $h) { $ok = $false }
    "{0,-34} 0005 marker={1}/1 code={2}" -f $c[0], $m, $(if ($h) {"OK"} else {"MISSING"})
  }
  foreach ($c in $p5) { & $py -c "import ast,sys; ast.parse(open(sys.argv[1],encoding='utf-8').read()); print('parse OK', sys.argv[1])" "$root\$($c[0])"; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { $ok = $false } }
  # patches 0001 / 0002 / 0004 must still be in place
  $p4 = [ordered]@{ "hermes_logging.py"=2; "agent\turn_context.py"=2; "agent\chat_completion_helpers.py"=2; "agent\stream_diag.py"=1; "agent\turn_recovery.py"=3; "agent\turn_finalizer.py"=1; "agent\turn_usage.py"=1; "gateway\platforms\api_server.py"=1 }
  foreach ($f in $p4.Keys) {
    $n = @(Select-String -Path "$root\$f" -Pattern "VYRON_LOCAL_PATCH_0004" -SimpleMatch).Count
    if ($n -ne $p4[$f]) { $ok = $false }
    "{0,-34} 0004 markers={1}/{2}" -f $f, $n, $p4[$f]
  }
  $p12 = [ordered]@{ "gateway\platforms\api_server.py"=1; "agent\agent_runtime_helpers.py"=1; "agent\turn_context.py"=1; "agent\turn_recovery.py"=2 }
  foreach ($f in $p12.Keys) {
    $n = @(Select-String -Path "$root\$f" -Pattern "VYRON_LOCAL_PATCH:" -SimpleMatch).Count
    if ($n -ne $p12[$f]) { $ok = $false }
    "{0,-34} 0001/0002 markers={1}/{2}" -f $f, $n, $p12[$f]
  }
  $flag = Select-String -Path "$root\gateway\platforms\api_server.py" -Pattern "agent._persist_disabled = True" -SimpleMatch -Quiet
  if (-not $flag) { $ok = $false }; "0001 persist flag line: $flag"
  if ($ok) { "RESULT: patch 0005 present and parses; 0001/0002/0004 intact - now restart the gateway" } else { "RESULT: NOT APPLIED CORRECTLY - do not restart; roll back or re-apply" }

  # After restarting, the running gateway must be newer than the newest patched file:
  ($p5 | ForEach-Object { (Get-Item "$root\$($_[0])").LastWriteTime } | Measure-Object -Maximum).Maximum
  (Get-Process -Id (Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 8642 -State Listen).OwningProcess).StartTime

HOW TO ROLL BACK (restores the newest 0005 backup of each file, then restart Hermes):

  $root  = "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent"
  $files = "agent\turn_usage.py","agent\codex_runtime.py","agent\session_persistence.py","agent\turn_facade.py","agent\conversation_loop.py","agent\agent_runtime_helpers.py","agent\background_review.py"
  foreach ($f in $files) {
    $dir = Split-Path "$root\$f"; $leaf = Split-Path $f -Leaf
    $bak = Get-ChildItem $dir -Filter "$leaf.vyron-pre-0005-*.bak" | Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1
    if ($bak) { Copy-Item $bak.FullName "$root\$f" -Force; "restored $f from $($bak.Name)" } else { Write-Warning "no 0005 backup found for $f" }
  }

